---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../config/site.ts';
import { tools } from '../data/tools.ts';
import { guides } from '../data/guides.ts';

const description =
  'PetCalc Tools builds free dog and cat calculators with cited formulas, lb and kg support, and clear limits. Learn who we are and how we work.';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About PetCalc Tools – Free Pet Calculators"
  description={description}
  canonicalPath="/about/"
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'About', path: '/about/' }]}
>
  <header class="hero">
    <h1>About {siteConfig.siteName}</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      {siteConfig.siteName} is a free set of dog and cat calculators for everyday decisions: how much to feed, how big a
      puppy will grow, how old a pet is in human terms, and when a situation needs a veterinarian right away.
    </p>
  </header>

  <div class="prose">
    <h2>What we do</h2>
    <p>
      Most pet owners meet the same handful of questions over and over. How many cups should my dog eat? Is this puppy
      going to be forty pounds or eighty? How worried should I be about the chocolate that disappeared from the
      counter? Search results for these questions tend to be a pile of ads wrapped around a rough rule of thumb.
      We built {siteConfig.siteName} to give you a direct answer first, then show the formula behind it so you can judge
      it for yourself.
    </p>
    <p>
      Every calculator runs in your browser. You do not need an account, and the numbers you type are not sent to a
      server by the calculator itself. Weights work in pounds or kilograms, results are shown in both, and every tool
      page explains the method, a worked example, common mistakes, and the sources behind the numbers.
    </p>

    <h2>What is here</h2>
    <p>
      There are {tools.length} calculators and {guides.length} long-form guides at launch. Dog tools cover puppy
      weight, dog and puppy food, homemade and raw portions, age, body condition, pregnancy due dates, chocolate
      toxicity, and water intake. Cat tools cover age and food. Browse the <a href="/tools/">full calculator list</a>,
      the <a href="/dogs/">dog hub</a>, the <a href="/cats/">cat hub</a>, or the <a href="/guides/">guides</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>How we keep content reliable</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Published formulas.</strong> Energy needs use resting energy requirement and life-stage multipliers
        taught in veterinary nutrition and described in the National Research Council's Nutrient Requirements of Dogs
        and Cats and the WSAVA Global Nutrition Guidelines.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Life stages from professional bodies.</strong> Age and life-stage content follows AAHA and AAFP
        guidance, and toxicity content follows ASPCA Animal Poison Control and the MSD Veterinary Manual.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Plain limits.</strong> Each page says what the tool cannot do. Calculators estimate; they do not
        diagnose, and they never replace an exam.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Dated pages.</strong> Every page shows when it was last updated. See our
        <a href="/methodology/">methodology</a> for the exact equations and editorial rules.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Veterinary review</h2>
    <p>
      We are working toward independent review of every page by a licensed veterinarian or board-certified
      nutritionist. Until a named reviewer is credited on a page, treat the content as general education that cites
      published guidelines, and use your own veterinarian as the final authority for your animal. Reviewer status is shown
      on each tool and guide page.
    </p>

    <h2>How the site is funded</h2>
    <p>
      The calculators are free. The site may show advertising through Google AdSense once an account is approved, and
      ads are always labelled and kept below the calculator so they never sit between you and your result. We do not sell
      pet food, supplements, or insurance, and we do not accept payment to change a calculation. Details of cookies and
      advertising are in the <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Corrections and feedback</h2>
    <p>
      If you spot an error, a broken link, or a number that does not match a source, please tell us through the
      <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>. Corrections are reviewed against the cited guideline and published with a new
      update date. You can meet the editorial team on the <a href="/authors/">authors page</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
